<title>USA: Boeing deal worth $62.89 per MD share.</title>
<headline>Boeing deal worth $62.89 per MD share.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders of McDonnell Douglas Corp will receive 0.65 shares of Boeing Co stock per share of MD they own, worth $62.89 at Friday's closing prices.</p>
<p>That represents about a 20 percent premium over McDonnell's closing price of $52. Shares of the Missouri-based aerospace firm gained $2-1/2 on Friday on volume of 463,000.</p>
<p>Boeing shares closed Friday at $96-3/4, up 1/2 on volume of 1.1 million.</p>
<p>--Aaron Pressman, 202-898-8312</p>
</text>
